---
// ── The problem ───────────────────────────────────────
---

<section class="section">
  <h2 class="h">Containers vs. VMs: pick your compromise</h2>
  <p class="section-desc" style="text-align:center;margin-bottom:1.75rem">
    Two ways to run software in isolation today — each asks you to give something up.
  </p>
  <div class="trio">
    <div class="pcard">
      <div class="name"><span class="dot d-gray"></span>Containers</div>
      <p>
        Fast and portable, but every container shares the host kernel. One kernel bug can cross the
        boundary.
      </p>
    </div>
    <div class="pcard">
      <div class="name"><span class="dot d-gold"></span>Traditional VMs</div>
      <p>
        Strong isolation, but heavy — and they boot through large UEFI firmware, a big,
        hard-to-reproduce trusted base.
      </p>
    </div>
    <div class="pcard win">
      <div class="name"><span class="dot d-green"></span>pichi</div>
      <p>
        Container-style workflow, true VM isolation, and a tiny boot chain with a deterministic
        launch measurement.
      </p>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<style>
  .trio {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: repeat(3, 1fr);
    gap: 1rem;
  }
  .pcard {
    background: var(--surface);
    border: 1px solid var(--border);
    border-radius: 8px;
    padding: 1.4rem;
  }
  .pcard.win {
    border-color: #2c5a2e;
    background: linear-gradient(180deg, rgba(63, 185, 80, 0.06), transparent);
  }
  .pcard .name {
    font-weight: 700;
    color: #fff;
    font-size: 1.05rem;
    margin-bottom: 0.5rem;
    display: flex;
    align-items: center;
    gap: 0.5rem;
  }
  .pcard .dot {
    width: 0.6rem;
    height: 0.6rem;
    border-radius: 50%;
    flex-shrink: 0;
  }
  .pcard p {
    font-size: 0.9rem;
    color: var(--muted);
    margin: 0;
  }
  .d-gray {
    background: var(--muted);
  }
  .d-gold {
    background: var(--gold);
  }
  .d-green {
    background: var(--green);
  }
</style>
